<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Central Bank bonds sold at 2.317 pct.</title>
<headline>Brazil Central Bank bonds sold at 2.317 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Central Bank sold 2.426 billion reais of 56-day Central Bank Bonds (BBC) Tuesday at an overnight call money rate of 2.317 percent a month, dealers said.</p>
<p>The rate at the bank's weekly formal bond auction was down from 2.348 percent at last week's sale.</p>
<p>The auction results show that 426 million reais will be drained from the banking system as 2.0 billion reais in 56-day old bonds are coming due Wednesday.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
